+# AUDIT — 2026-10-15 duplicate/conflict sweep (`supremeai-open`)
+
+> **Auditor:** external autonomous contributor agent (fork/PR + direct-push lane; AGENTS.md §2.1)
+> **Method:** full read of every tracked file family (5 workflows, 3 issue templates, 2 Python
+> programs, 5 docs, README, ECOSYSTEM_MAP, AGENTS/AGENT_RULES, the entire
+> `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/` tree, api-schemas, examples), plus live verification via
+> `gh`, local test reproduction against `origin/main` (`git worktree`), and the canonical validator.
+> Auditor policy §3 applied: every finding was verified before filing, checked against existing
+> issues/PRs for duplicates, and filed as an atomic slice with root cause, evidence, and a
+> smallest-safe-change proposal.
+
+## Context: a second sweep on the same day
+
+Issue #95 recorded the 2026-10-15 deep audit (8 findings, #86–#93). Between that audit and this
+sweep, PRs #99–#105 landed fixes for #87–#93 and the board grew again. This sweep therefore:
+
+1. **did not re-file** anything covered by #86–#95, #98, or the fleet-filed set;
+2. swept **new surfaces** (test wiring, redaction SSOT, doc-contract duplication, guard matching
+   semantics, board integrity) and filed **7 new findings (#116–#123)**;
+3. recorded verified **no-actionable-finding** results below (AGENT_RULES §10).
+
